  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In the SDK I found it's far too easy to obtain other people's avatars. Wanting to build a useful tool with the SDK I want to respect the author's intention with the avatar.\n\nPlease add an option to add a \"policy\" to an avatar description.\nIt should contain at least:\n- Public\n- Private\n\nNice to have might include:\n- Whitelist usernames\n(To address uploading avatars for friends)\n- Whitelist worlds\n(For particular games / RP)\n\nAnother nice to have would be to have clients actually enforce this policy by turning voilations into the red avatar instead. And to disable pedestals that have private avatars set to them. (What's the point of \"stealing\" an avatar when nobody can see it?)\n\nHowever, if only this information was added to avatars ASAP, even just as text in the API without any enforcement, creators can make their intentions clear and it would allow developers to respect their wishes.",
